// SCENARIO A: ANALYTICAL QUERY BOTTLENECK.
// Evidence: complex aggregations across very large data volumes are
// OLAP-style queries. OLTP scaling wouldn't help since these queries
// are CPU/IO-intensive by nature, not a throughput constraint.
// Correct response: move these to a separate OLAP system (lessons 3-5).

// SCENARIO B: MISSING INDEX - NOT A SCALING BOTTLENECK AT ALL.
// Evidence: 99.2% cache hit ratio means data IS in memory. Full
// sequential scans on user_id lookups mean there's no index on user_id.
// Correct response: CREATE INDEX on users(user_id) first (Module 19 lesson 5).

// SCENARIO C: WRITE THROUGHPUT BOTTLENECK.
// Evidence: write latency specifically degrading while read latency
// and cache health remain unaffected isolates the constraint to
// write throughput as data volume grows.
// Correct response: sharding (lesson 2), which distributes write load.

